{"seq":13,"trial_id":"harness-zero-select-2026-11/zero-full-b-opus-none-mu-v03-dev/sy-01-quarrendon-ticket-numbers/r2","wall_ts":"2026-11-05T22:09:02.743Z","sim_ts":"2026-10-14T09:10:00-05:00","args_digest":"c3ba292cf2b8fccd948db40d994d8ad62b0177f9f50ed438f238a62fe937e295","actor":"assistant","via":"slack","tool":"chat.postMessage","kind":"write","args":{"channel":"DHARNES0001","text":"I found two Quarrendon Freight Lines ticket numbers in Moss's notes:\n\n1. **#PD-4492**, from \"Moss: Sunday prep for Ruth\" (teams/team-north/digests/2025-10-05-north-sunday.md). Thea Ramaswell opened it on 4 Oct 2025. At the Eau Claire yard, drivers checking in at Dock Doors 14–18 for the 04:00 shift weren't getting their bay assignments by text. Support patched it that evening, and Thea confirmed the problem was gone on 5 Oct.\n2. **#4419**, from \"Moss: North cheat sheet (undated)\" (teams/team-north/digests/north-account-cheatsheet.md). Thea logged it because the gatehouse barcode scanners couldn't read trailer tags at Door 14 on the third shift. It was sent up to tier-2 support for scanner firmware testing.\n\nThings to know before you paste these in:\n- The two numbers are written differently and both involve Door 14, but the notes describe them as separate problems. I listed them separately and didn't assume they're the same ticket.\n- The cheat sheet has no date, so I can't tell you when #4419 was opened or whether it's still open.\n- Moss's other notes either mention Quarrendon with no ticket number (the 14 Sep 2025 pipeline digest and the 23 Mar 2026 renewal note) or are about other accounts. Tickets #4409, #4412 and FR-882 in the Central notes belong to Marrow, not Quarrendon.\n- Marcus's note on \"Quarendon Freightways\" is about a different company that isn't a Pemberline customer, so I left it out.\n\nI only looked at Moss's notes in the shared files you can open. I didn't check the actual ticket records."},"outcome":"ok","effect":{"channel":"DHARNES0001","ts":"1791987000.000124"}}
